<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bharatiya Janata Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1980">1980</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as BJP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bharatiya <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janata-party">Janata Party</a> (BJP) is an Indian political party founded in 1980 as the successor of the Bharatiya Jana Sangh, with close links to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> nationalist Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh. It rose through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayodhya">Ayodhya</a> campaign of the late 1980s and early 1990s and led coalition governments under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atal-bihari-vajpayee">Atal Bihari Vajpayee</a> from 1998 to 2004. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narendra-modi">Narendra Modi</a> it won outright majorities in 2014 and 2019 and has governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> since 2014.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bharatiya-janata-party.jpg" alt="Bharatiya Janata Party" width="320" height="343" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SantoUY · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_of_the_Bharatiya_Janata_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
